{
  "about": "The off-screen SDRAM rows Player 2 uses (T0 of the Talos plan, D-T05). Engine word addresses are row * 512 + column; rows 0..359 are the visible framebuffer (columns 400..511 of every row are the engine's own markers, never pixels), rows 360..1023 are the stash, shared by both display buffers. A new user of the stash adds its rows here and in fw2/gfx/gfx.h; sim/test_sdram_map_fw2.py reads the C constants named below and refuses an overlap or a constant that drifted from this file.",
  "stride": 512,
  "visible_rows": 360,
  "total_rows": 1024,
  "pixel_cols": 400,
  "double_buffer": {
    "base_words": 1048576,
    "rtl": "src/fpga/core/mp3_fb.sv DBUF_BASE1",
    "c": "fw2/gfx/gfx.c DBUF_BASE1_W",
    "note": "2 MiB, inside the CPU's uncached window (starts at 1 MiB); fw2 never touches SDRAM through that window, so nothing writes it but the engine and the mailbox"
  },
